:: 3.1. Hallway [nobr] {"position":"500,1100","size":"100,100"}
<<showAgent "exception">>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "hallway1">>
        You step into the corridor. It is long. Strange light. Then: movement ahead. An alien — the Exception — drifts at the far end, not approaching, not retreating. Just present.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The narrator goes quiet. First contact begins
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Small distortions. Crystal rustling. The biochip adjusts its functions to speech.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        What is the true intent behind it? You're trying to be understood. Is that what you call intent, or does our definition differ?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [["Hey, can you understand what I am saying?"|3.1. Choice A]]
			[["I guess you can understand me..? What am I even doing here?"|3.1. Choice B]]
			[["How is it that I escaped so easily?"|3.1. Choice C]]
			[["I heard a voice telling me that I was kidnapped here by fellow humans and that I am here to be researched on. So what is the end goal here?"|3.1. Choice Voice]]
            [[Don't mind me, just passing through.|3.1. Passing Through]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>



:: 3.1. Human Voice [nobr agent] {"position":"625,1900","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.HumanVoice">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Frequency. Composition. The particular arrangement of signals that characterises your species and Earthly lifeform in general. But this communication is distinct from anything else we have catalogued. It is also the only voice on this vessel that modulates when it believes it is not being observed. Otherwise, there's no reason to modulate on the vessel.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[What has the voice been saying?|3.1. Voice Saying]]
            [[Do you mean it just sounds human or is it an actual human saying it?|3.1. Actually Human]]
            [[Where do I go from here?|3.1. Where Go]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>



:: 3.1. No Consent [nobr agent] {"position":"125,2275","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.NoConsent">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Will as a variable in the exchange having any effect, not will in general. Although.. how do you think being aware of it would affect the current circumstances?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The answer goes nowhere you can follow. There is nothing to do but move.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue into the hallway.|Hallway Convergence]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>



:: 3.1. Passing Through [nobr] {"position":"600,1200","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "passingThrough">>
        You walk past slowly. The alien doesn't turn around. It doesn't need to — it feels your passing presence without needing to look
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You sigh.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        I can't believe that worked.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue into the hallway.|Hallway Convergence]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>



:: 3.1. Punch [nobr] {"position":"562.5,2350","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.Punch">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        You swing. Your hand connects with something that is not like flesh. The alien doesn't react. Your hand does.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You retreat, shaking your fingers. The alien stands exactly as it was.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Walk it off. Continue into the hallway.|Hallway Convergence]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>



:: 3.1. Sold Against Will [nobr agent] {"position":"275,2100","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "3.1.SoldAgainstWill">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Sold. A transfer of ownership contingent on the assignation of value to a living organism. The concept of will as a variable in such exchanges is not something we have encountered.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[You don't know the concept of will? You could have just said you don't care about my consent instead of beating around a bush.|3.1. No Consent]]
            [[So you didn't even consider me potentially being uncompliant about this? Have you never done something you didn't want to do?|3.1. Uncompliant]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>



