        "I don't know. The hallway is long.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue into the hallway.|Hallway Convergence]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>



:: 3.2. Able Or Want [nobr contact] {"position":"900,1400","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "ableOrWant">>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
    	Because we don't want to. Earth is yet too dangerous to step on. Careful research is still in order.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
			[["How is Earth dangerous to you?"|3.2. Earth Dangerous]]
            [["I think I understand, somehow."|3.2. What Now]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: 3.2. Alien Arrival [nobr contact] {"position":"500,1500","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "alienArrival">>
        Three aliens enter: the Cartographer, the Analyst, and the Engineer. They keep their distance, arms extending inquisitively
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
            They are the ones who put you in here, but not the ones who got you aboard this ship. Their nature is incompatible with anything that could harm you in this very moment. You needn't fret.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
            Subject is in a conversational state. Could the subject not have understood the instructive oscillation carvings of his waking chamber? Or was there some other reason for the meeting arrangement?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The three researchers observe you, waiting.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[What is going on here? What are you?|3.2. What Are You]]
			[[What do you want from me?|3.2. What Want]]
			[[Why did you release me?|3.2. Why Released]]
			[[Yeah, I could understand it. I was just wondering what would happen if I pressed the wrong button.|3.2. Wrong Button]]
            [[So, am I free to go now?|3.2. Free To Go]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>



:: 3.2. Earth Dangerous [nobr contact] {"position":"900,1600","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "earthDangerous">>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
    	The entropy is at its highest observed display within the system. Life itself poses more of a threat than other consequential interactions. Life and death are intertwined so tightly that life never truly ends. Any outlandish objects will find themselves either consumed or becoming part of the local ecosystem.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [["I think I understand, somehow."|3.2. What Now]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: 3.2. Free To Go [nobr contact] {"position":"800,1450","size":"100,200"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "freeToGo">>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
    	The departure for your home planet is unavailable as of the moment. The subject will stay on the ship until further notice.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
			[["Are you not able to bring me back, or do you not want to?"|3.2. Able Or Want]]
            [["So you completed the transaction — what can I do now?"|3.2. What Now]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: 3.2. Humanity Warning [nobr contact] {"position":"1000,1500","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "humanityWarning">>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
        Notable correction. Assuming its 'intent' carried through. But upon observing human behaviour further, an augmentation of behaviour tracking may serve the research more.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [["If your kind can detect this intent.. let's just say you may not be that far off."|3.2. Not Far Off]]
            [["Can never have too many warnings when dealing with humans."|3.2. Narrator Goodbye]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: 3.2. Narrator Goodbye [nobr] {"position":"1200,1450","size":"100,200"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "narratorGoodbye">>
        The three aliens disperse. You step into the hallway. The narrator speaks.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        That ended surprisingly well. All three of the signal carriers came to aid you. Remember their likeness, for you will need them if you want out of this place. With them not being so eager to help you out in your time of need, just use their observational nature for your own gain. You're near the end of this comically long hallway.. Ahead is a room where things actually listen to will.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue down the hallway.|Hallway Convergence]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



