<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "notFarOff">>
        Dialog??
        <div class="choice">
            [[Head into the hallway.|3.2. Narrator Goodbye]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: 3.2. Risk Lives [nobr contact] {"position":"1000,1400","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "riskLives">>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
    	Precisely. It's a risk — only evaluating the risk remains. Knowledge gathered on this expedition is unique to this one.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [["Alright, I'll try not to break anything."|3.2. Narrator Goodbye]]
            [["Better make sure the risk doesn't outweigh that knowledge. You have no idea what humanity is capable of."|3.2. Humanity Warning]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: 3.2. What Are You [nobr contact] {"position":"700,1350","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "whatAreYou">>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
    	This vessel is a research instrument. We are the researchers. You are from the third orbital body of this system, called Earth. A world whose life patterns we have been cataloguing for some time. The patterns we see follow a path full of disturbance.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Cartographer">>
    	What you are, in our current framework, is unprecedented. A living conversational piece of the Deathworld you inhabit.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
			[[What do you want from me?|3.2. What Want]]
			[[Why did you release me?|3.2. Why Released]]
			[[Yeah, I could understand it. I was just wondering what would happen if I pressed the wrong button.|3.2. Wrong Button]]
            [[So, am I free to go now?|3.2. Free To Go]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: 3.2. What Now [nobr contact] {"position":"900,1500","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "whatNow">>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
    	The movement is as restricted as your being allows. It's an experiment we all designated to partake in.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [["You're all part of the experiment? You'd risk your lives just to observe me?"|3.2. Risk Lives]]
            [["Let me explore this ship then."|3.2. Narrator Goodbye]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: 3.2. What Want [nobr contact] {"position":"700,1450","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "whatWant">>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
    	Want implies desire contingent on absence. Absence is absent.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
    	What does your presence allow us to observe that was not observable before? The answer is considerable.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
			[[What is going on here? What are you?|3.2. What Are You]]
			[[Why did you release me?|3.2. Why Released]]
			[[Yeah, I could understand it. I was just wondering what would happen if I pressed the wrong button.|3.2. Wrong Button]]
            [[So, am I free to go now?|3.2. Free To Go]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: 3.2. Why Released [nobr contact] {"position":"700,1550","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "whyReleased">>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
    	Released implies prior restraint imposed with intent. The chamber was a stabilisation environment — a functional requirement of the transfer process, not a containment measure.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
    	You were not held. You were maintained and adapted.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Analyst">>
        The distinction appears significant to you. We are noting that.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
			[[What is going on here? What are you?|3.2. What Are You]]
			[[What do you want from me?|3.2. What Want]]
			[[Yeah, I could understand it. I was just wondering what would happen if I pressed the wrong button.|3.2. Wrong Button]]
            [[So, am I free to go now?|3.2. Free To Go]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: 3.2. Wrong Button [nobr contact] {"position":"700,1650","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "wrongButton">>
        <<speaker "Engineer">>
    	An experiment. You introduced a variable deviation into a process specifically designed to remove variables.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Engineer">>
    	The resulting outcome — this meeting — was less efficient than the designed outcome but produced equivalent data. Possibly more.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Engineer">>
        This approach is similar to methods previously observed. Earth seems to thrive in uncertainty.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
			[[What is going on here? What are you?|3.2. What Are You]]
			[[What do you want from me?|3.2. What Want]]
			[[Why did you release me?|3.2. Why Released]]
            [[So, am I free to go now?|3.2. Free To Go]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Analyst Dead End Hallway [nobr] {"position":"2200,1500","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "analystDeadEndHallway">>
        You head back out of the specimen bay, retracing your steps toward the long hallway where you first came from. The narrator is talking about the engineering bay. He doesn't stop.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You slow down. The wall panels here don't all sit flush. One in particular — you wouldn't notice it if you weren't looking. Behind it: something small. Not alien-made. The biochip doesn't translate it because it doesn't need to. Human hands shaped this. A device with a single dial and four positions, each marked with a symbol the biochip renders as a section of the ship. One position is already turned. Three are not.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The narrator is still talking. He doesn't know you've stopped.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Pick up the device and continue to engineering.|Artifact Picked Up]]
            [[Leave it and continue to engineering.|Engineering Bay Entry]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



