<</script>>

<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "archiveException">>
    	<<speaker "Narrator">>
        ... This one is more important than that one.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You approach anyway.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        Hey, is that you again? You all look so similar.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Why is it that you remembered me? You are seeking a pattern where your species usually sees only noise.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        That's not even true. What do you even know about my species?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Fair enough.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        What's your deal? What do you do here?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Nothing in particular. I observe the observers. What do you do here?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        I don't even know. I can only really follow the voice in my head. I'm not presented with much choice so far.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Presented? You're actively looking for choices. But presented is a loose word.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The Exception gestures toward the view of Earth below.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Using your eyes, looking at the world below.. What do you think of?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Conversation Ended|Archive Bay Entry]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Archive Terminal [nobr] {"position":"1800,300","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "archiveTerminal">>
        In 2071, we stopped feeling alone.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Unannounced and unprovoked, a structure several times larger than any space station appeared in low orbit, locking over the Pacific. Governments classified it immediately. They had other things to manage — a decade of war had already stretched trust to its thinnest point, and a revelation of this scale would have broken what remained.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        By 2079 practically everyone knew anyway. By 2137 until now seventeen governments have fallen. The ones that didn't were absorbed into something calling itself a federation. And in the gaps left behind, other things grew. They always do. Criminal networks. Shadow organisations with no names you'd recognise but reach you'd find impressive. Some of them made contact with the visitors. Not diplomatically as much as commercially.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The visitors, as it turns out, are curious about us. Curious enough to have stayed for decades. Curious enough to want samples. The kind of samples that don't come from soil or atmosphere.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        [ END OF DOCUMENT ]
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Hm. I haven't seen that written down before. Whoever put that there has a flair for the dramatic. Or they just wanted someone to find it. Possibly both.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Return to the archive bay.|Archive Bay Entry]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Artifact Control Disable [nobr] {"position":"3200,1500","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "artifactControlDisable">>
        You walk back to the Engineering bay. Not to speak with the Engineer — you approach the workbench where you showed it the device. The fourth position on the dial: a symbol the biochip renders as CONTROL ROOM. You adjust it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        What are you— what are you doing? What do you have?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The control room security systems reduce. A low tone sounds through the ship.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Stop. Stop. I need you to stop right now.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        When he speaks again the philosophical register is gone. Harder. Faster.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Alright. Listen to me. I know what that does. I know you think you've just changed the shape of this. You haven't. You've changed one variable and I have been in this room for a very long time and I know this room better than the device you're holding knows it. Come to the control room. We can still do this the way it was supposed to go.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You leave the engineering bay and walk back through the long hallway toward the central room and the control room door.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Walk to the control room now.|Failed Artifact Ending]]
            [[Emit the Exception's signal before entering.|Artifact Signal Check]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Artifact End Final [nobr] {"position":"3700,1700","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "artifactEndShould">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        What happens now is yours. I can't stop you. The room is yours. The panel is there. Whatever you do next, I want you to know that this—
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        He gestures vaguely at the space between you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        This wasn't what I planned. But I find I'm not sorry it happened this way. That surprises me.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Place hand on panel.|Ending A Skepticism]]
            [[Leave him there. Walk out.|Artifact End Walk Out]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Artifact End Should [nobr] {"position":"3600,1800","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "artifactEndShould">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Yes. I should have. I catalogued everything on this ship and I looked at that particular alien and filed it as incidental. That's the kind of error you make when you're alone for too long and start to think you've mapped everything.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Artifact End Final]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Artifact End Walk Out [nobr] {"position":"3900,1800","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "artifactEndShould">>
        You leave. The narrator remains on the floor of his own control room. He doesn't call after you. The Exception is in the hallway.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        You found the blind spot.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        I have been waiting to see if anyone would. The first one didn't. I wasn't certain you would either. I'm glad I was wrong.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It falls into step beside you. Not leading. Not following. Beside.)It falls into step beside you. Not leading. Not following. Beside.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The ship reached navigational independence at 04:52 UTC.
        A signal inconsistent with standard biochip transmission was recorded at 04:49 UTC.
        Its origin was not identified.
        It was not filed.
        The Exception was noted as absent from its usual observation position.
        It was not searched for.
        The researcher filed a full report.
        He described the subject as “cooperative.”
        He used the word carefully, the way people use words they know aren’t quite right but can’t find better ones for.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[End.|Game Over]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Artifact End Wanted [nobr] {"position":"3600,1700","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "artifactEndWatch">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Did it? Did it want this or did it just provide information and let you decide? That distinction matters to it. It told you that, I imagine. Want implies an absence it's trying to fill. Maybe it did want it. Maybe that's what it looks like when it wants something.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Artifact End Final]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Artifact End Watch [nobr] {"position":"3600,1600","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "artifactEndWatch">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Yes. I see that now. Watching me watch you. Waiting for someone to come through this ship and be worth handing a blind spot to. That's actually extraordinary. I don't have another word for it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Artifact End Final]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Artifact Picked Up [nobr] {"position":"2300,1500","size":"100,100"}
