:: Awakening Chamber [nobr waking] {"position":"200,1300","size":"100,100"}
<<audio awakening play>>
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "awakeningChamber">>
	    Water drains. Disorientation. You are awake before you understand what that means.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
	    Okay. You're awake. That's the hard part done, for both of us honestly.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
	    You're not on Earth. I know that's a lot to absorb in the first five seconds. Take a breath. The environment is stable.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
	    There are two buttons in front of you. Hit the right one. It opens the exit seal. The left one runs a pressure check you don't need — I've watched people stare at those symbols for twenty minutes and it doesn't get more interesting, I promise you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
	    The right button reads: EXIT. The left button reads: ENTER.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Press the right button — EXIT.|Right Button]]
			[[Press the left button — ENTER.|Left Button]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>


:: Burn Activation [nobr] {"position":"2800,3050","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnActivation">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Wait.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Not a command. The word a person uses when they are out of arguments and down to bare wire.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I know what you're going to do. I know I can't stop you. I want to say something before you do it. Not to change your mind. Just. I need you to hear something.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Say it.|Burn Say It]]
            [[No.|Burn No]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Burn Exception Activation [nobr] {"position":"2800,2650","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnExceptionActivation">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Wait.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        His voice cuts in for the first time since you entered this section.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I know what you're going to do. I know I can't stop you. I want to say something before you do it. Not to change your mind. Just. I need you to hear something."
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Say it.|Burn Exception Say It]]
            [[No.|Burn Exception Panel]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Burn Exception Led [nobr] {"position":"2600,2600","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnExceptionLed">>
        <<speaker "You">>
        You led me here on purpose.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        I provided information. What you did with it was your own.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        That's not an answer.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        No. I led you here on purpose. You asked for an answer so there it is. I observed the first person and I did not intervene and they died and I have been holding that as a variable without a function for a long time. You are not them. But you are the same kind of thing. I wanted to see if the outcome could be different.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "You">>
        Is it?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        You are standing in the Fusion Core. You are alive. You are making a choice. That is already different.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[What do you want me to do?|Burn Exception What]]
            [[I'm going to destroy this ship.|Burn Exception Activation]]
            [[Walk away.|Burn Exception Walk]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Burn Exception Narrator [nobr] {"position":"2600,2500","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnExceptionNarrator">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        In the control room. He cannot reach this part of the ship. The frequency he uses to keep the others out also keeps him in. I wondered how long it would take him to notice that. It has been longer than I expected.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You came.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[You led me here on purpose.|Burn Exception Led]]
            [[What do you want me to do?|Burn Exception What]]
            [[I'm going to destroy this ship.|Burn Exception Activation]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Burn Exception Panel [nobr] {"position":"3200,2600","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnExceptionPanel">>
        You press the panel. A low tone.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Is that— is it in there with you?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        A pause.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Of course it is. I spent months watching it drift through this ship like it had nowhere to be. I thought it was nothing. Just an extra. I thought I was the interesting one.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        A long beat. Then, very quietly:
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Well played. I mean that.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Burn Final]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Burn Exception Say It [nobr] {"position":"3000,2600","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnExceptionSayIt">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I have spent a long time believing that humanity is worth something. Not in the abstract — I mean specifically worth it. I believed that if I could just get out of this room and get this ship moving then something would change. For the argument. For the idea that we deserve to be part of whatever this is. And maybe I was wrong. Maybe the thing I was trying to prove is exactly what I disproved by trying to prove it. I love this species. I love it completely. Even right now. Even this.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Press the panel.|Burn Exception Panel]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Burn Exception Walk [nobr] {"position":"2800,2550","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnExceptionWhat">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Then walk away.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        It steps aside. No further comment. You arrive at the control room. The narrator is surprised — you took the long way around. He finds this, unexpectedly, moving.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Place hand on panel.|Ending A Curiosity]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Burn Exception What [nobr] {"position":"2600,2700","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnExceptionWhat">>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        I want nothing. Want implies an absence I'm trying to fill. I told you that. But I will tell you what I observe. The voice in your head has been in that room for a long time. Long enough to stop being a person in some ways that matter. Long enough to stop being able to see the difference between using someone and helping them. The ship holds data that has taken decades to gather. The voice needs you to leave this room and walk to the control room and place your hand on a panel.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Beat.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        There is also a panel here.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[I'm going to destroy this ship.|Burn Exception Activation]]
            [[Walk away.|Burn Exception Walk]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Burn Final [nobr] {"position":"3400,2800","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnFinal">>
        The four-minute countdown is not displayed as a number. It is felt. The heat changes. The hum shifts register. The lights don't flicker — they clarify, briefly, as the systems maximise before they fail.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        I have been observing for a very long time. I have observed birth and continuation and the end of both. I have never observed something choose. Not like this. Not with full information and no survival pressure and the ability to walk away.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        A pause. Something in its register that is as close to warmth as it gets.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        Your species is genuinely the strangest thing in this system. I will not be able to tell anyone that. But I know it now. That seems like enough.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The ship ends. The research ends. The narrator ends. The Exception ends, with its particular form of patience. You end — not because of the biochip this time, but because you chose a thing larger than the biochip.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Blackout.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The ship was observed to descend from its orbital position at 03:14 UTC.
        No distress signal was recorded.
        No wreckage was recovered.
        The research consortium filed a report attributing the loss to navigational failure.
        The Exception's absence from the vessel was not noted in the report.
        It had not been listed as a research subject.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[End.|Game Over]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Burn Narrator Body [nobr] {"position":"2600,3000","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnNarratorBody">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Because something prevented it. The ship's systems don't refuse. They don't make exceptions. Something would have had to actively—
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        He stops. His voice, for the first time, has no cadence to it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Something kept that body there. Something wanted you to find it. Something wanted you to have a reason to…
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        He looks at the controls behind you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I have been in this room because the frequency keeps the aliens out. I told you that. I did not tell you I could also not leave. The frequency works in both directions. I have been in this room for a very long time. And something has been watching me be in it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[You were used too.|Burn Narrator Used]]
            [[I'm going to destroy this ship.|Burn Activation]]
            [[Walk away with me.|Burn Walk Away]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Burn Narrator Knew [nobr] {"position":"2600,2900","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "burnNarratorKnew">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I knew they died. I did not know the body was still there. I want that distinction to mean something and I understand if it doesn't.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Why did the ship not process the body?|Burn Narrator Body]]
            [[I'm going to destroy this ship.|Burn Activation]]
            [[Walk away with me.|Burn Walk Away]]
