:: Discarded Room First [nobr missing-features] {"position":"2000,700","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "discardedRoomFirst">>
    	The discarded room sits off the archive, slightly recessed. No signage the biochip translates. The door opens. Inside: dim, still air. The smell of something that has had a long time to become what it is. In the far corner, a body. Human. It looks as rotted as it can in this sterile environment.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The narrator goes quiet. Not the reflective quiet he uses when he wants you to feel the weight of something. A different kind.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        That shouldn't be there. I mean the body. Ah shit.. There was a person before you. Someone else who came through the same process. They didn't survive it, their biochip malfunctioned. That part I knew. What I didn't know was that they were in here somehow. I assumed the ship's biological systems would have processed them. The ship processes everything eventually. That's just… how it works.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        A beat. When he speaks again he is slightly too quick.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Believe me, there's nothing relevant in there. Come out. You still have signals to gather.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The room is the same. The body is the same. But the Exception is standing here. Not near the body. On the other side of it. Still. As if it has been here for a long time.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Exception">>
        You came back.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The room is the same. The body is the same. There is nothing new here. The narrator says nothing.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Who were they?|Discarded Who]]
            [[Did you do this?|Discarded Did You]]
            [[I don't want to be in here.|Discarded Leave]]
            [[Talk to Exception|Discarded Exception]]
            [[Return to the archive.|Archive Bay Entry]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Discarded Who [nobr] {"position":"2100,600","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "discardedWho">>
    	<<speaker "Narrator">>
        Someone like you. Same process, but a different outcome. They were frightened before I could finish explaining anything. It moved faster than I anticipated. I knew they died. But they certainly can't have died here.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Pause. Then, a beat too soon.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        This may look important to you and in a way it is, but in a way that you should hurry up.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Return to the archive.|Archive Bay Entry]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Ending A Agression [nobr] {"position":"4500,0","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "endingACuriosity">>
        You place your hand on the panel.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Alright. I expected you to make me work for that. I had arguments prepared. Contingencies. You didn't make me use any of them. I think that's more frightening than if you had. A person who's been angry this whole time and still chooses to help — I don't have a framework for that. The aliens don't either. I checked.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Don't tell anyone I said that.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Death A]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Ending A Choice [nobr missing-dialog missing-features] {"position":"4200,300","size":"100,200"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "endingAChoice">>
        Chosing ending variant A
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[A Compliance|Ending A Compliance]]
            [[A Skepticism|Ending A Skepticism]]
            [[A Curiosity|Ending A Curiosity]]
            [[A Agression|Ending A Agression]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Ending A Compliance [nobr] {"position":"4500,200","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "endingACompliance">>
        You place your hand on the panel. The screens light up. He leans forward — the posture of a person doing the thing they have been trying to do for a very long time.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Alright. Yes. Good. I had a whole thing prepared about trust. About how it's the mechanism underneath everything your species builds. It was quite good, I think. But you're here and the ship is moving and I find I just— I hope it's somewhere you chose. Where you end up. I hope at some point in the next part of things there is a place you arrive at because you wanted to and not because someone routed you there.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        He says this to the screens. Not to you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Death A]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Ending A Curiosity [nobr] {"position":"4500,700","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "endingACuriosity">>
        You place your hand on the panel. The ship hums. The narrator exhales.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Right. Good. That's— yes. I have been thinking about this moment for a long time. I had a thing I was going to say. Something about curiosity and human nature and what it proves about the species. I have had a great deal of time to compose it. It's gone. I can't find it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Thank you. For coming through the door. I mean that precisely and without anything else attached to it.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Death A]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Ending A Skepticism [nobr] {"position":"4500,500","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "endingASkepticism">>
        You place your hand on the panel. The screens come alive.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You knew. You knew what I was doing and what it cost and what I wasn't telling you and you did it anyway. I want to understand that. I've been watching humanity for years and I still want to understand that. I think it might be the most important thing your species does. Acting without complete information because the alternative is standing still. You just — you move. Even when you don't know where.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Thank you for moving.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Death A]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Ending B [nobr missing-features] {"position":"4200,1000","size":"100,200"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "endingB">>
        <<speaker "You">>
        What happens to me after you have the ship?
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I take you back to Earth. That was always part of it. I am not in the business of collecting people, I'm in the business of getting from one place to another, and you are not a destination for me. You are someone who got caught in something larger than yourself through no particular fault and you deserve to be on the ground again. I cannot give you back the time. I can give you the planet.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[I believe you. Place hand on panel.|Ending B Believe]]
            [[I don't. But I'm doing it anyway. Place hand on panel.|Ending B Skeptic]]
            [[Your organisation. Will they come for me when we get back?|Ending B Organisation]]
            [[Was there anything on this ship you're glad I saw?|Ending B Glad]]
            [[Why should I believe you'll actually take me back?|Ending B Trust]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Ending B Believe [nobr] {"position":"4600,900","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "endingBBelieve">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I know. Somewhere along the way you decided I was worth that. I'm not sure I deserved it but I find myself grateful for it regardless, which tells me something about the nature of gratitude that I hadn't quite figured out before. There is more humanity in that word — believe — than any of the aliens have managed to document in all their years of research. The act of choosing to believe someone without proof. It's profoundly strange. It's profoundly human.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You place your hand on the panel. The ship responds.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Death A]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Ending B Glad [nobr] {"position":"4400,1050","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "endingBGlad">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Can I ask you something? You don't have to answer.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        He watches your face. He doesn't finish the question. He doesn't need to.)
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I thought so. Me too. I've been trying to remember that.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Place hand on panel.|Ending B Believe]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Ending B Organisation [nobr] {"position":"4400,950","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "endingBOrganization">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I don't know the current status of the organisation. I've been in this room. But I want to tell you something about them — about us. We were very good at finding people who could handle things we needed handled and then not thinking too carefully about what it cost those people. I think you should go somewhere they won't find you, at least for a while. I think you've earned that.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Place hand on panel.|Ending B Believe]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Ending B Skeptic [nobr] {"position":"4600,1200","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "endingBSkeptic">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Ha. Yes. Alright. That's the most honest thing anyone has said to me in quite some time. The aliens mean everything they say or they mean nothing. There's no room in between. You're doing the thing in between. Acting on something unresolved. I respect that more than I probably should, given the circumstances. Come on. Let's see if this works.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        He turns to the controls. The ship responds.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Continue.|Death A]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Ending B Trust [nobr] {"position":"4400,1150","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "endingBTrust">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You shouldn't, on the basis of evidence. On the basis of evidence I've lied by omission, manipulated your path through this ship, and gotten one person killed. Those are the facts. What I can tell you is that I need you alive to operate this ship, and once we're moving, your continued existence stops being a logistical requirement and becomes a choice. I'm choosing it. I know that's not proof. It's what I have.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        He watches your face. He doesn't finish the question. He doesn't need to.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I thought so. Me too. I've been trying to remember that.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[I believe you. Place hand on panel.|Ending B Believe]]
            [[I don't. But I'm doing it anyway.|Ending B Skeptic]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



