:: Engineering Bay Entry [nobr missing-features] {"position":"1800,2100","size":"100,200"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "engineeringBayEntry">>
        The door. Strange signs above it. The biochip activates, rendering their meaning directly into your understanding: Engineering.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        There it is. Go talk to it. This one seems to deal in the practical — how things work, what they're used for. It would make sense to go along with those lines.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Well now you know what to do I guess. And if you have ever wondered why in the hell you're even doing all of this, just try and do something else besides this. Yeah this is pretty much it. You're free to take it as a challenge though.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Oh yeah, good luck by the way.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You found it then. The other one. I was wondering when you would. I'll be honest with you, I thought you might handle it worse than this. People usually fall apart when they find out they're not the first. But here you are. Still moving. Still asking questions. That's the thing about you that keeps surprising me, and I have thought about this ship's interior quite a lot. More time than I would like to admit, really. Now you know the full picture. Go get that last signal and come back to the door. I won't waste more of your time.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You're a smooth sailor. Just letting you know.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        A small, well-lit room. Shelf-like containers line the walls. Three workbenches at the centre. The Engineer is present, engrossed in its work, not acknowledging you
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The device is still in your hand. The Engineer hasn't noticed yet.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [["Greetings."|Eng Route A]]
            [[Stand and wait to be acknowledged.|Eng Route B]]
            [[Explore the room quietly.|Eng Route C]]
            [[Move closer behind it.|Eng Route D]]
            [[Show the Engineer the device.|Eng Artifact Request]]
            [[I want to see the Fusion Core.|Fusion Core Request]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Failed Artifact Ending [nobr] {"position":"3400,1500","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "failedArtifactEnding">>
        You walk to the control room. The door opens. The narrator is standing. Not seated. He has been waiting. The looseness is gone from him. He is a person who has made a decision.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The biochip malfunctions harder in this room than before.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I want to explain something to you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        He moves to the side of the room — not toward you, not away. A deliberate positioning.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I have been in this room for a long time. Long enough to learn every system on this ship. Long enough to understand what that device does and what it doesn't do and what I put in place specifically because I knew — I knew — that someone might find it. That someone might try this.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I'm sorry. I need you to know that I mean that.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        He does something. The biochip distorts the moment. You fall.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        You are not dead yet. The floor of the control room is cold. The screens above are alive. He crouches down. Close. His voice is quiet now.  
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You were clever. You were genuinely clever. The device, the hallway, the Engineer — that was a path I put in place as a contingency and you found it and you walked it and I want you to know that means something. It means you were exactly what I needed you to be and exactly what I was afraid of, which in my experience is usually the same person.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Maya did something like this. Not the same. But the same shape. She found a way to refuse that I hadn't accounted for. I thought I had learned from that. Maybe I learned the wrong thing.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Your vision narrows.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You deserved a better version of this. I love this species. Even right now. Especially right now. I don't know what to do with that.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        Darkness.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The ship reached navigational independence at 04:52 UTC.
        No distress signal was recorded.
        The subject's biochip had ceased transmission.
        It was filed as equipment failure.
        The device found in the long hallway was not recovered.
        It was not listed in any manifest.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[End.|Game Over]]
        </div> 
  <</ctp>>
</div>



