:: Left Button [nobr room1] {"position":"400,1500","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "leftButton">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Evidently, the goods don't need to pass many regulation checks to end up here. Don't worry, everything is still fine, but you just made things less adaptively convenient for yourself.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        The pressure check is harmless. Just takes a moment longer.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Alright, well.. Things would have been easier if you met these things outside of this pod on your own terms, but I can assure you that they will do you no harm regardless thankfully. The door will open shortly. Not from your side.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        When it does, you're going to see something in the corridor that will look alarming. Don't make sudden or unprovoked moves. You will just stay in there now and meet your observers who should know enough about you to just simply release you from this on their own accord.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The door opens from outside. You wait.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Wait and see what enters.|3.2. Alien Arrival]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>



:: Narrator Identity [nobr] {"position":"1500,800","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "narratorIdentity">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I talk through the means the aliens designated for cases such as this. I help guide you in this dire predicament. I know enough things to keep being useful to you. Now you're likely referring to something more basic — maybe even about the very nature of my existence. 
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Am I an alien, a human or even a program? You wouldn't be crazy to be thinking I am any of these.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        But that's not what I want from you. I have desire that's much better defined. You've probably already realised that the ones you've met so far don't quite operate on the same principles you're used to.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        What both me and you want is inside the room ahead. The room ahead of you — the one that's currently locked — it's not part of their usual routine.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        It's an exception.. Much like yourself, in a way.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [["You still haven't told me who you are."|Narrator Who Are You]]
            [["What do you want me to do?"|Narrator What To Do]]
            [["Why can't you just open the door yourself?"|Narrator Why Not Open]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Narrator What To Do [nobr] {"position":"1600,800","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "narratorWhatToDo">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You're going to move through the adjacent sections of the ship. Each of them serves a purpose. Each of them contains something you'll need.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You don't have to understand everything you see. You just need to remember it. Then when you have all three parts of the access code complete, come back to this very room and unlock the door in front of you.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [["Why can't you just open the door yourself?"|Narrator Why Not Open]]
            [[Head to the bays.|Pre Control Room]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



