  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Narrator Why Not Open [nobr] {"position":"1600,900","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "narratorWhyNotOpen">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You're the one who acts here — not even the aliens can take that away from you. Make use of your humanity, which is always available to you, and give the aliens a little wake-up call. Find out what it is they hide in this room specifically.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        And when you do, humanity will have won.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Head to the bays.|Pre Control Room]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Pre Control Room [nobr missing-features] {"position":"1500,1250","size":"200,200"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "preControlRoom">>
        A large room. A gateway door directly opposite — locked. Three paths branch from here.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        It's definitely locked. It does seem like a way to go doesn't it? But this isn't the only way to go from here. There are three additional paths that diverge from this room — think of all of them as serving a functional purpose relating to the alien's research.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Go talk to them. Specifically the three signal carriers. Each of them should be in their respective rooms right now and certainly aren't hard to miss.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        You have all three signals. Come back to the door. Everything after this is mine to explain.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        The door remains locked. The three paths wait.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Approach the locked door and enter the code.|Code Entry]]
            [[Head to the Archive bay.|Archive Bay Entry]]
            [[Return to the Archive bay.|Archive Bay Return]]
            [[Head to the Specimen bay.|Specimen Bay Entry]]
            [[Head to the Engineering bay.|Engineering Bay Entry]]
            [["Hold up. Who or what even are you?"|Narrator Identity]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>>
</div>



:: Right Button [nobr room1] {"position":"400,1100","size":"100,100"}
<div class="textbox">
    <<ctp "rightButton">>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
	    You're feeling alive and well thankfully, that's one hurdle down. Now you need to move on from this room as there are some visitors.. you may not immediately recognise as conversable. But it's better to meet them on your own terms.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
	    The door ahead of you will open in a moment. Step through when you're ready.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
	    You're not on Earth. I know that's a lot to absorb in the first five seconds. Take a breath. The environment is stable.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
	    I should explain where you are. You're aboard a vessel. Not a human one. I know how that sounds. I need you to stay calm while I walk you through what's happened, because it's going to sound alarming and it isn't.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        What you're going to see in the corridor is going to be strange. I need you to remember that strange doesn't mean dangerous.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        I'll explain everything once you're moving ahead, that's how confident I am that you're going to be present in the next room and room after that.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <<speaker "Narrator">>
        Just follow the general directions.
    <<ctpNext clear>>
        <div class="choice">
            [[Step through the door.|3.1. Hallway]]
        </div>
  <</ctp>> 
</div>



